#. type: Title #
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:1 docs/sap/security-model.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "SAP Security"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:8
msgid ""
"Hub RPC requires a **service API token** on every WebSocket `connect`. SAP "
"attach still assumes a trusted client once transport auth succeeds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trust boundary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (mermaid)
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"flowchart TB\n"
"  subgraph trusted [Trusted client with service token]\n"
"    Hub[\"Hub anima service :2658\"]\n"
"    RpcEndpoint[\"/hub/rpc/v1 WebSocket\"]\n"
"    Bundled[Bundled SPA modules]\n"
"    SatA[Satellite companion]\n"
"    SatB[Satellite pair-programming]\n"
"  end\n"
"  Browser[Browser]\n"
"  Browser --> Bundled\n"
"  Browser --> SatA\n"
"  Bundled -->|\"HubRPC connect + auth_token\"| RpcEndpoint\n"
"  SatA -->|\"HubRPC + sap.attach\"| RpcEndpoint\n"
"  SatB --> RpcEndpoint\n"
"  RpcEndpoint --> Hub\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Current controls"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Control                       | Status                                                 |\n"
"| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| TLS on Hub RPC                | Optional; remote access via Tunnel + HTTPS/WSS         |\n"
"| Token on Hub RPC `connect`    | **Yes** — service API token (`verifyServiceApiToken`)  |\n"
"| Origin check on WebSocket     | **None**                                               |\n"
"| SAP attach for instance scope | **Yes** — `tool.*` requires `sap.attach`               |\n"
"| Session-scoped tool routing   | **Yes** — [strict routing](tools.md)                   |\n"
"| Credential values in frames   | **No** — credentials stay in pass; LLM sees paths only |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:41
msgid ""
"Any client that holds a valid service token and can reach `ws://"
"127.0.0.1:2658/hub/rpc/v1` can:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:44
msgid ""
"Call bundled RPC methods (chat, tasks, notifications, …) without `sap.attach`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:44
msgid ""
"After `sap.attach`, register tools as the attached `app_id` / `instance_id`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:46
msgid ""
"Operational guidance: bind Hub to loopback; rotate service tokens; do not "
"expose port 2658 to untrusted networks without Tunnel + Access. See "
"[security guide](../guide/security.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "Protocol hardening (transport layer)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/security-model.md:50
msgid ""
"Invalid frames close the socket with **1003**. Protocol violations (double "
"connect, RPC before connect, `tool.*` without attach) close with **1008**. "
"Failed auth closes with **1008** (`unauthorized`)."
msgstr ""

